From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: accept the 7.2 remain_on_channel rx address

Linux 7.2 adds a const u8 *rx_addr argument to cfg80211_ops
.remain_on_channel. The vendored mac80211 still installs the 7.1
prototype, so cfg.c fails to build:

  cfg.c:4294:30: error: initialization of 'int (*)(struct wiphy *, struct
  wireless_dev *, struct ieee80211_channel *, unsigned int, u64 *,
  const u8 *)' from incompatible pointer type 'int (*)(struct wiphy *,
  struct wireless_dev *, struct ieee80211_channel *, unsigned int,
  u64 *)' [-Wincompatible-pointer-types]

Guard the extra argument on the kernel version. The driver has no use
for a per-peer ROC yet, so the address is ignored.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
diff --git a/hal_apollo/mac80211/cfg.c b/hal_apollo/mac80211/cfg.c
--- a/hal_apollo/mac80211/cfg.c
+++ b/hal_apollo/mac80211/cfg.c
@@ -3312,7 +3312,11 @@
 				       enum nl80211_channel_type channel_type,
 				       #endif
 				       unsigned int duration,
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7,2,0))
+				       u64 *cookie, const u8 *rx_addr)
+#else
 				       u64 *cookie)
+#endif
 {
 #if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3,6,0))
 	struct net_device *dev = wdev_to_ndev(wdev);
@@ -3320,6 +3324,9 @@
 #if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(3,8,0))
     enum nl80211_channel_type channel_type = NL80211_CHAN_HT20;
 #endif
+#if (LINUX_VERSION_CODE >= KERNEL_VERSION(7,2,0))
+	(void)rx_addr;
+#endif
 	struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata = IEEE80211_DEV_TO_SUB_IF(dev);
 	struct ieee80211_local *local = sdata->local;
 	int ret;
